From 19636c8d717c104cd943933db8482ca5e03e61d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andras Lasso <lasso@queensu.ca>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:46:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] ENH: Compute automatic segment opacities for binary
 labelmap representation

Automatic opacity computation (making segments that contain other
segments translucent, so that the inner segments are visible) only worked
when the 3D views showed poly data: the topological hierarchy was built
from the poly data of each segment. When binary labelmap is shown in 3D
views (as surfaces computed on the GPU) no poly data was collected, so
the computation failed with an error, and segmentations loaded from
labelmap-only files never got automatic opacities.

The hierarchy only uses the bounding box of each segment, so
vtkMRMLSegmentationDisplayNode::CalculateAutoOpacitiesForSegments now
computes the bounds of each segment from the displayed representation:
poly data, or the voxels of the segment in the (shared) labelmap, found
by vtkOrientedImageDataResample::CalculateEffectiveExtentPerLabel in one
pass per labelmap and transformed to world coordinates. Segments without
voxels take no part in the hierarchy and stay opaque. The preferred
representation is only created if nothing can be shown in 3D views yet,
so computing the opacities does not convert a segmentation that is
already displayable.

The labelmap surface rendering snaps translucent opacities to a few
levels. The number of levels is now a property of the display node
(NumberOfLabelmapSurfaceOpacityLevels, default 5, minimum 3, saved in
the scene), used by the displayable manager instead of a constant, and by
the automatic opacity computation, which distributes the hierarchy levels
among the available opacity levels and stores the opacities that are
actually rendered (so that what is stored in the display node is what is
shown).

vtkSlicerSegmentationsModuleLogic::LoadSegmentationFromFile computes
automatic opacities when the representation shown in 3D views is in the
file (closed surface, or binary labelmap if that is shown in 3D), so
loading still does not trigger a conversion.

vtkMRMLSegmentationNodeTest1 checks automatic opacities for nested
segments of a shared labelmap, shown as labelmap and as closed surface,
for a segment without voxels, and the effect of the number of opacity
levels.
